WEBVTT

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.280
With the rapid development of Hyper Technology came the Labor...

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.380
a multi-purpose, humanoid construction machine whose use...

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.290
spread into almost every field.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:23.330
However, this gave rise to a new threat to society: Labor crime.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:31.310
The Tokyo Metro Police founded the Special Vehicles, Section 2...

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.440
within the Security Division to combat these ever-growing crimes.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:42.490
This was the beginning of the SV2 Patrol Labor... Patlabor... units.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:03.080
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:09.560
HAATO BIITO wo awaserya sore de ikisou yo
If I can get my heartbeat under control, I think I'll make it

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:15.270
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:20.910
takaku hayaku suki yo ki mama ni
Higher, faster, I'll love you if I want to

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:27.460
METARU BODII no hadazawari sae
I think I'll get to like

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:33.400
atsuku kanjite kuru kuse ni narisou
The way I get flushed at the touch of your metal body

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:39.690
CHACHI na Imagination koeta jigen de
Oh, don't stop this gravity-defying feeling

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:46.580
juuryokuihan ah nukeru Feeling tomenai de
That goes way beyond mere imagination

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:53.100
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:59.550
PITAri kakarerya PIKAA kireru ARUFONSU
When I hold him tight, my Alphonse can do anything

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:05.180
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:13.760
sora mo umi mo kyou mo ashita mo Nothin' impossible
Anytime, anywhere, nothing's impossible

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.720
Nothing's impossible

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.530
Report from 7th Precinct Security Headquarters:

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.700
707 in progress at Jinnan Town, Shibuya Ward!

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.340
Criminal is using a civil engineering Labor, and is heavily armed!

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.780
SV2, all units launch! SV2, all units launch!

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.450
That's...

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.600
What the...

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.400
There are <i>wings</i> on that Labor's back!

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.730
Don't tell me it can...

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:03.300
The Patrol Labor AV-2.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.780
A power booster, fixed wings, and a propulsion device are attached...

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.210
to a standard Labor, making aerial maneuvering possible.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.280
Captain!

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.010
This overcomes the weakness of old Labors, which could only operate...

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.320
over long distances with the aid of a trailer, and gives us the...

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.550
ability to combat aerial crimes, which will come in the near future.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.790
The top brass accepted your proposal...

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:26.020
and Sakaki and Shige worked all night to finish it.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.530
Way to go, Izumi!

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.120
Leave the ground control to us, Noa!

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.300
Thanks, Captain! Sakaki!

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.270
You, too, Shige! Thanks, everybody!

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.460
What's wrong, Noa?

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.930
Propulsion! I'm losing propulsion!

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.500
I can't gain any altitude!

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.200
Your wings! Flap your wings, Noa!

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.710
Say <i>what?</i> I'm going down!

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.140
It's falling! Run!

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:25.520
I thought so.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.300
I knew it was too good to be true.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:44.270
No kidding, Noa. It'll be another ten years before Labors will fly.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.640
Unbelievable.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:52.240
And that "power booster" thing... You sure have classic dreams.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.310
Anyway, who's the big shot...

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:59.450
that I got dragged out of bed to pick up?

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.890
I'm supposed to be off today.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:04.430
An NYPD police sergeant by the name of Kanuka Clancy.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.160
"Kanuka"? Weird name.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:11.000
She's a third-generation Hawaiian emigrant, I hear.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:15.410
So why's this Kanuka lady coming to Tokyo?

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:18.000
Is she coming to the SV2?

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:21.580
What, you think I know everything?

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:22.740
Yeah.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:25.720
Look, there's talk that the mayor of New York...

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:29.190
might be coming to visit Tokyo, right?

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:32.950
It probably has something to do with security for that.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:37.020
But to come in through Yokota Air Base on a U.S. military plane...

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:40.760
I dunno... I get a weird feeling that this is something big.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.250
I <i>knew</i> it'd be something like this.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.260
You said you had a <i>bad</i> feeling about this.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.330
- I still do.
- Oh.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:18.360
And so...

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:22.460
given the importance of security during the New York mayor's stay here...

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:26.070
the mobilization of the SV2 has been requested, as well.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:30.110
And on that note, I'd now like to introduce Sgt. Kanuka Clancy...

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:35.950
who was rushed here this morning to deliver some important information.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:38.720
Sgt. Clancy?

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.760
Wow! English!

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.790
Just yesterday, Japan time, we...

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:54.740
Wow! Japanese!

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:57.310
- I'm in love!
- She's fluent!

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.980
We received information to the effect that the Terror Network...

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.740
was going to try something during the mayor's stay here.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:09.010
So when's their mayor coming?

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.090
Today at 4.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.320
Geez! It's a little late, isn't it?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.720
This information is still under investigation...

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.890
but because it was leaked by an arms dealer we had arrested...

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.260
who wanted to deal, we believe it's reliability to be rather high.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:26.500
According to Interpol, the following Terror Network members...

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:28.970
are hiding throughout the world.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.710
Hey. What's the "Terror Network"?

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:32.800
Don't look at <i>me!</i>

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.980
It's one of those groups where they table their differences...

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.810
in philosophy and join forces to accomplish their goals.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.720
- What do you mean?
- It's a terrorist mutual aid society.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.390
And these are the objectives of the mayor's visit here:

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:48.790
Aside from it being a goodwill visit to our Sister City...

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:51.760
he will also see the Babylon Project. In short...

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.700
You're saying that it's very likely...

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.260
that Beach House is sponsoring what's coming.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.440
That's what we're thinking.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:05.440
What the heck are the Babylon Project and Beach House?

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.540
You joined the force and you don't even know that?

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:10.240
It ain't like I joined because I <i>wanted</i> to.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:11.910
- What?
- What?

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:14.480
Well, the Babylon Project is...

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:18.050
more than just an extraordinary construction project to protect...

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:21.680
the bay from rising sea levels caused by the greenhouse effect.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:24.990
It'll seal off the entire bay area, build giant sluices...

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.230
and over the course of 50 years, reclaim that land...

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.790
solving the Metro area's land problems in one blow.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.970
But there's a lot of opposition, saying that it's a reckless plan...

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:38.640
that ignores the impact on ocean currents and the bay's ecosystem.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.800
The opposition efforts of the countless extremist...

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:43.350
environmental protection groups is growing stronger.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:47.220
Among these, "Beach House" was the first to make a call to arms...

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.580
and they began to carry out acts of terrorism in the capital last year.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:53.090
They're the extremists among extremists, so to speak...

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:56.160
and are the thorn in the Public Security Department's side.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:09:01.130
But despite all that, construction really took off last year...

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:04.430
and because of the project, the number of construction Labors...

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.700
in the capital jumped by a factor of 87.

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:09.970
As a result, Labor crimes also rose, which was the reason behind...

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:13.840
the founding of the Patrol Labor squads.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.340
Wow, you sure know a lot.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:18.970
No. Anybody who reads the papers every day would know that much.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.180
- Yeah, <i>everybody</i> knows that.
- Well, you got me.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.410
I guess I sound like a complete idiot, <i>don't</i> I?

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:24.920
Aren't you?

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.020
Quiet!

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:36.020
That's all the information we have at present.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.100
- What's your number?
- What're your measurements?

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.200
Do you have any sisters?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.940
Shut up!

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.330
Unit 2 here. Runway inspection complete.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:11.390
Good. The 4th Mechanized Squad is guarding finger 13, Unit 2.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.900
- Meet them and back up Squad C.
- Roger!

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:16.500
You're really going all-out.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:21.380
Even if I mobilize all my backup cars, I only have three Labors...

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:24.010
and there are countless points we need to check.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.880
But if they want to strike at the moment that'll be most effective as...

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:30.620
anti-Babylon Project propaganda.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:35.590
Right. The luncheon with the Tokyo Governor at noon tomorrow.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.660
If it were me, that's what <i>I'd</i> go for.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:41.360
What's the main security force around the Diet building?

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:44.770
Fifty SP Unit members under HQ's direct command...

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.600
who specialize in security for VIPs...

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:51.070
along with 200 members of the elite 2nd Riot Squad: "Hell's 2nd".

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.810
And of course, the members of our own beloved Second Unit.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.390
Hey! What do you think you're doing?

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:08.890
Keep it moving, you pinhead!

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:10.380
Move it, scumbag!

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.900
The Tohoku, Kan'etsu, Chuou, and Toumei Expressways...

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.630
the #3 Keihin, the Keiou, and then there's the regular highways.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:22.300
Even the <i>entire</i> police force couldn't handle all this traffic!

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.540
It's no wonder the drivers are ticked off!

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.630
Geez, what the hell were the top brass thinking?

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.710
Well, he's the city's guest.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:31.010
Their pride wouldn't let them call in units...

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.240
from other police departments as backup.

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:37.380
But we're never gonna be loved by the citizens as <i>their</i> police force!

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:40.460
Yo, cops! Yeah, you two! Get to work!

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.720
Say <i>what?</i> You bastard!

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.430
It sure is quiet.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.800
And here they're saying that there are traffic jams all over the city...

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:50.560
and there's even rioting in some places.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:53.900
That's because this area's closed off to all but police traffic.

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:56.340
Heck, we ought to take it easy while we can.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:12:00.610
But the main security force is those SP guys, right?

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:04.770
Yeah. So how come Kanuka Clancy is working with a Labor unit...

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.510
when she's Security, same as those guys?

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.420
Something's fishy here.

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:11.250
The answer: She likes Labors!

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:14.630
You shouldn't apply your standards to everybody else.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:19.250
<i>What?</i> Most people would call <i>this</i> goofing off!

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.960
Don't be stupid. Like you can work on an empty stomach.

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:23.430
That hit the spot.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:25.060
Hey! Where are you going?

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.430
The john!

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:33.380
He eats, he goes to the bathroom. This guy just can't handle stress.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:36.950
There's one!

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:38.640
Mister!

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:42.590
Me?

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.850
Are you a policeman?

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.220
Yeah, but I try not to stand out.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.690
Then do something about that!

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:51.090
"That"?

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:56.090
It's a big pain, having something like that sitting there, Mister!

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:57.960
Is that a mobile command center?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:02.930
Do you know that the mayor of New York is coming, Ma'am?

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.170
No.

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:09.150
Well, he <i>is!</i> Anyway, we need that to keep him safe while he's here.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.940
So you can't do anything about it?

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:12.020
No.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:14.210
Then who <i>can?</i>

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:15.950
Nobody!

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.620
Be good, now. Just go home and pet your cat, okay?

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.220
It's not good for you to be wandering around here.

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:23.290
'Bye!

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.420
Fine! See if I care!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:31.290
Kids today, they ought to learn to listen to what people tell them.

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:50.800
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:55.810
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.860
The time is now 10:35.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:15.460
The mayor of New York and his party are now safely in their rooms...

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:19.470
at the Hotel New Otani, in a Tokyo that is on full alert.

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:22.100
His departure was delayed because of a bomb threat...

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:25.110
and then, among other problems, his jet had engine trouble...

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.150
so he arrived nearly six hours behind schedule.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.680
We're reporting to you from above the Hotel New Otani.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.120
Back to you in the studio, Tawaura.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:35.320
Thank you for that live report.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.010
Now, focusing on the harsh criticism that...

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:42.590
the security measures for this visit are clearly excessive...

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:47.260
And <i>I'd</i> like to focus on this excessive <i>work...</i>

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:51.130
This means that we'll be sent out again tomorrow morning, doesn't it?

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:54.570
The First Unit will be working security all night...

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:57.770
at the New Otani again tonight!

00:14:58.010 --> 00:14:59.340
They're lucky.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:03.680
The First Unit gets the New Otani, and we just get <i>this.</i>

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.450
They'll just be standing outside all night, that's all.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:07.820
Is Shinshi here?

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.150
Your wife dropped this off a while ago.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:12.280
She said it's a change of underwear.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.290
- Thanks.
- Ow!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.320
I'd better call.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.800
I hate you, you loving husband you!

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.800
Ladykiller!

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.540
The privileges of being a married man.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.970
Pansy!

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:29.070
Can somebody go out and buy us some dinner?

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:32.010
C'mon, Captain! Why didn't you say something earlier?

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.010
We could've stopped and got something on our way back!

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.480
Like we could park our command cars and carriers...

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.380
in front of a mini-mart, you moron.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:41.420
Noa! Get me some instant <i>tanmen</i> with fried octopus in it.

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:43.620
Why are you telling <i>me</i> that?

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.820
I'll go, Noa.

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:47.250
Lend me your scooter.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:52.500
If you love that scooter of yours, <i>you</i> go. There's a good girl.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:54.160
Could you get me some socks, too?

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:56.100
One of those valu-packs with three pairs for $3.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.670
Okay, okay!

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.330
Let's have the requests!

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:02.670
Five rice balls! And some Okakama mayo and extra-bitter sea chicken.

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:05.270
Get me some oolong tea; the convenience store brand.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:09.370
Three curry muffins, the kind with soy pickles in them. And some...

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:12.040
I can't take this down if you're all talking at once!

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:14.380
Oh, you're getting dinner? I'll have...

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.190
Melon-jam muffins and instant soup, right?

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:31.700
Freeze. One move and you're dead.

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:33.570
I'll drop you where you stand.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.650
Oh, Shinobu.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:21.220
Geez, I'm sleepy.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:23.450
Not enough sleep, Shinohara?

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:26.790
I had this awful dream where I was buried alive under a mountain...

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:30.260
of smelly socks, and my face was being eaten away by athlete's foot.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.520
Same here.

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:35.590
Sleep if you want, but do it with your eyes open. And don't drool.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:39.000
There's no telling where the press is hiding, snapping pictures.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:40.540
Yes, sir.

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:45.040
But there's no point in standing guard here, Captain!

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:49.050
The helicopter's landing on the far roof of the Diet building, right?

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:51.510
We have our orders.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:54.180
This spot will be the most photogenic when they show it...

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:56.480
on the monitors over at Security Headquarters.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:18:01.990
Zero-One to Zero-Zero. Observation complete. Now returning. Over!

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:06.330
Zero-Zero, roger. Metro security shows all clear.

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:12.000
Zero-One, your ETA at the Diet building is 1200 hours.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:16.670
It's time to go to the reception hall, sir.

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:20.810
They're not the Strategic Air Force or Spectre.

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:24.720
It's sick to get all googly-eyed over something on a monitor.

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:27.620
Geez, it's <i>always</i> us grunts who get shafted.

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:30.620
I mean, if they're gonna make a mobile command center like that...

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:33.090
they could at least come down and <i>use</i> it once.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:34.680
Mobile command center?

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.800
What are you talking about?

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.160
I saw it yesterday.

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:42.960
It was in Central Park, smack in front of the Diet building.

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:46.400
It was a trailer, with a big "Metro Police" written on the side.

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:48.740
- We have one, right?
- Nope.

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:52.440
The department doesn't have anything like that!

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:54.670
What <i>is</i> it, then?

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:58.910
Noa! Wake up, Noa!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:02.110
Shinohara! Hey! What's going on?

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:05.560
I'll tell you later! Get the bomb squad on the horn!

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.030
Come on, Noa!

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:11.370
Where are you going?

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.460
This is the SV2, Second Unit in front of the Diet building.

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:16.900
Come in, headquarters.

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.160
This is Zero-One.

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:22.210
Now passing over Trade Center building at Hamamatsu. Over.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:31.550
If that's what I think it is...

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:33.980
Stop! Stop!

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:39.220
What's the problem?

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.850
I can't get past this!

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:46.000
- Can't you go under it somehow?
- It's too low!

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:49.560
Damn! Too tall to walk over, too low to go under.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:56.400
To the blimp passing overhead! This is an emergency!

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:58.480
This is Officer Shinohara, Unit 1 commander...

00:19:58.580 --> 00:19:59.740
with the SV2's Second Unit!

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:01.710
What?

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.920
You can't be serious!

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:06.750
I'm telling you, this is an emergency!

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.550
Okay, you got it! I'll give it a shot!

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:14.450
Noa! Grab that blimp that's on its way down!

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.360
I'm gonna let you fly, just like you wanted!

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:20.220
What am I supposed to grab on to?

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:21.730
Think of something!

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.770
If anything happens, it's <i>your</i> fault!

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:29.300
Don't do it, Captain!

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:32.870
Can it! I've always wanted to try something like this!

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:34.780
I don't care if it costs me my license!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:38.420
Police

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:45.580
Hold on tight, now!

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:50.100
It's not working! I'm not going up!

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:51.860
Kick off from the ground!

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:58.040
You did it!

00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:23.820
My sensor's picking up a quartz transmitter and micro-motor sounds!

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:32.740
Listen closely, Shinohara.

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:37.140
Half an hour ago, the bomb squad went out to deal with a launcher...

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:41.340
identical to yours that was found parked in a lot in Nakano-Fujimi.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:44.380
They determined that it was a dummy...

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:48.650
but assuming they set the timer for the mayor's landing time...

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:50.720
there's about 10 minutes left.

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:53.620
Even if they tried to get to you, they'd never make it in time.

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:56.360
Then tell them to send back the helicopter! Hurry!

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:59.230
"The luncheon will proceed as planned.

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:02.500
Canceling it would disgrace the department, so that's impossible.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.430
Do whatever it takes to resolve the situation..."

00:22:05.540 --> 00:22:07.940
is what the Top Brass have said.

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:10.770
That's crazy! What am I supposed to do?

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:13.440
Dismantle it.

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:15.010
Captain?

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:20.110
Do it! Or do you want me to have Izumi do it?

00:22:20.490 --> 00:22:22.650
You're the one who drew out the old lady.

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:24.450
We don't have any cards left to play.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:28.720
Captain Nagumo is on her way there with Sgt. Clancy.

00:22:28.830 --> 00:22:31.730
She says she's had training in explosives disposal at the NYPD.

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:33.960
Do what she tells you to do from here on in.

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:42.030
So it's a trailer-style launcher with a timing mechanism?

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:45.940
Then I think it's the same type that was used in LA two months ago.

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:49.810
Officer Izumi. Start by removing the trailer's exterior.

00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:53.090
Small vibrations aren't a problem, but if the launcher's...

00:22:53.190 --> 00:22:56.520
heading or angle is changed, it'll go off, so be careful.

00:22:56.620 --> 00:22:57.590
Roger!

00:23:10.400 --> 00:23:13.500
It's hopeless! I can't defuse this monster!

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:17.610
I'm just a public servant that took Labor command training!

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:22.180
Calm down! All of that overblown gadgetry is a decoy.

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:24.350
It's a dummy that's there to distract you.

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:25.610
The real mechanism is...

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:35.090
Found it!

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:37.660
There are four screws holding the cover.

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:41.260
Unscrew them one at a time, going counter-clockwise from the upper left.

00:23:42.140 --> 00:23:44.930
But the screws themselves go clockwise!

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:51.410
Okay, it's cut.

00:23:51.510 --> 00:23:54.950
Okay, next is the backup power insulator.

00:23:55.280 --> 00:23:57.480
Take the yellow wire that's going up...

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:59.640
from the relay switch in the upper right.

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:01.880
Wait, hold up! There are <i>two</i> yellow wires here!

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:03.580
There shouldn't be!

00:24:03.860 --> 00:24:05.020
Well, there <i>are!</i>

00:24:27.110 --> 00:24:28.880
Okay, two wires left.

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:31.080
Listen closely. You're almost done.

00:24:31.550 --> 00:24:33.140
There's a red wire and a blue wire.

00:24:33.250 --> 00:24:36.150
They both go out from the clock and into a cylinder.

00:24:36.260 --> 00:24:38.090
- Right?
- Right.

00:24:39.360 --> 00:24:42.630
Red or blue? Which don't you like?

00:24:42.930 --> 00:24:44.400
Um... Red, I guess.

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:46.260
Then cut the red wire.

00:24:46.370 --> 00:24:48.730
Hold on! What are you talking about?

00:24:48.840 --> 00:24:51.070
One wire is the insulated wire to the detonator.

00:24:51.170 --> 00:24:54.200
The other is a dummy that's linked to the trigger.

00:24:54.410 --> 00:24:56.770
Only the guy who built it knows which is which.

00:24:56.880 --> 00:24:58.900
You have a 50% chance.

00:24:59.010 --> 00:25:03.280
But if I don't pick one of them, time will run out, and BOOM.

00:25:03.880 --> 00:25:05.220
This sucks!

00:25:13.530 --> 00:25:16.500
What's that word in English where you have a <i>big</i> bet...

00:25:16.600 --> 00:25:19.030
where you have to leave everything up to chance?

00:25:19.130 --> 00:25:20.120
Long shot.

00:25:29.480 --> 00:25:31.880
Which one would <i>you</i> cut, Noa?

00:25:31.980 --> 00:25:35.510
H-How should <i>I</i> know?

00:25:36.320 --> 00:25:39.650
You're right. There's no way <i>to</i> know!

00:25:46.260 --> 00:25:49.060
Please, God. Help us.

00:25:49.160 --> 00:25:50.960
Help us. Help us.

00:26:16.590 --> 00:26:20.820
Thank you, God! Thank you!

00:26:29.340 --> 00:26:32.270
Ine "The Gadget" Ito. Age 72.

00:26:32.370 --> 00:26:35.430
Wanted internationally for a total of 22 violations...

00:26:35.540 --> 00:26:37.370
of explosives handling laws.

00:26:37.740 --> 00:26:40.110
That's one scary old lady.

00:26:40.210 --> 00:26:42.240
If I ever run into her again, I'll kill her!

00:26:42.350 --> 00:26:45.650
If you had done your job and looked through those wanted flyers...

00:26:45.750 --> 00:26:47.450
this wouldn't have happened!

00:26:47.550 --> 00:26:49.390
Yeah, you're right.

00:26:49.560 --> 00:26:52.020
It doesn't matter, anyway. I'm gonna quit.

00:26:53.030 --> 00:26:54.990
You really want to quit?

00:26:55.100 --> 00:26:59.030
It's been three days now, and my heart's <i>still</i> pounding.

00:26:59.730 --> 00:27:01.960
Captain! I'm gonna quit! Do you hear me?

00:27:02.070 --> 00:27:05.400
Fine, just so long as I get a written resignation.

00:27:05.510 --> 00:27:08.670
You <i>are</i> the hero of all this though.

00:27:09.180 --> 00:27:12.480
Good, it looks like you're all here, gentlemen.

00:27:13.280 --> 00:27:15.110
Allow me to re-introduce our guest...

00:27:15.220 --> 00:27:18.580
who has just has been assigned here for a one-year study period.

00:27:18.690 --> 00:27:21.590
Sergeant Kanuka Clancy. Take good care of her.

00:27:23.760 --> 00:27:24.750
I quit.

00:27:24.860 --> 00:27:26.620
Huh? Did you say something?

00:27:26.830 --> 00:27:29.390
I won't try to quit anymore.

00:27:29.500 --> 00:27:33.230
Forget what I said, okay, Captain?

00:27:41.760 --> 00:27:46.600
Long Shot

00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:44.700
An unknown giant creature appears in Tokyo Bay.

00:28:44.810 --> 00:28:47.170
Is it the wrath of God? The illegitimate spawn of the Devil?

00:28:47.270 --> 00:28:49.800
And what is the horrible, secret research of the genius scientist...

00:28:49.910 --> 00:28:50.880
Professor Hirata?

00:28:50.980 --> 00:28:53.740
It's calling! Tokyo Bay is calling Alphonse!

00:28:53.850 --> 00:28:56.410
Next time! The 450 Million Year Old Trap!

00:28:56.780 --> 00:28:58.440
Target, lock on!
